  "notes": "Almost always written in kana. The object is nearly always ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧ (hair).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive (⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧).\n- Pattern: ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧とかす\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧とかす: comb one's hair\n- くし⟦で→で：00502_de⟧とかす: comb with a comb\n- ⟦ブラシ→ブラシ：01503_burashi⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧とかす: brush through\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{溶|と}かす→溶かす：08264_tokasu⟧: to melt; to dissolve — same reading but a different verb (heat or liquid). Context makes the meaning clear.",
